SAME PLACE? The runtime walk: `(p-flush-dropped-handle %h)` -> `%p-flush-dropped-value` walks the container's DIRECT elements (one level, +p-flush-walk-limit+ = 64) and flushes a handle there; for `undef $obj` the walk starts at the scalar, so the hash it refers to is the one level.  For a cleared container the one level is the container's own elements, so a handle inside an element's referent is level two.  Direction: the walk depth is a parameter -- a cleared aggregate walks its elements' referents one level (the same 64-element bound per level), measured for cost on a `%h = ()` of 10 / 10,000 keys.  NOT taken in s543m (a resume begins nothing new).


